{
    "name": "E2E Spotify - playlist lifecycle",
    "description": "End-to-end test for the Spotify connector - creates a playlist, finds a track, replaces and appends playlist items, lists playlists and items, then deletes the playlist.",
    "type": "automation",
    "notes": {
        "d8bbcf05-216c-4240-bce3-c4f9dfbe1fe4": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 880,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThis flow provokes all of its own data: **Create Playlist** makes a private playlist named `E2E Spotify Lifecycle <OnStart time>` and **Delete Playlist** removes it again after `AfterAll`, so nothing has to pre-exist on the tenant.\n\nTwo things must hold on the connected account:\n\n1. **Find Tracks** searches the live Spotify catalogue for `The Beatles` / `Hey Jude` with `minScore 0.5`. If Spotify returns no match the component emits on `notFound` and the chain stalls until the `AfterAll` timeout.\n2. The Spotify app is likely in **Development Mode**: it serves at most 5 users, each added by hand in the app's User Management, and stops working when the app owner's Spotify Premium subscription lapses. A 403 on every component means the E2E account is not on that list."
        }
    },
